/// REFUSE: A positional argument may not follow a named one.
///
/// Issue #15.  Positional arguments come first; after the first named argument
/// every remaining one must be named.
///
/// ⚠️ This file is refused TODAY, and for the wrong reason -- '=>' does not
/// scan, so it dies at 'Expect expression!' rather than at the rule.  That is
/// precisely why the oracle checks the sentence and not merely the exit code: a
/// harness asking only whether the program failed would report this as already
/// correct, and would go on doing so after the feature landed.
///
/// The signature deliberately carries no default, so that nothing in it is
/// refused ahead of the call and the reported sentence is the call's.
///
function Slice (Text : String, Start : Integer) : String;
begin
    Exit Copy (Text, Start, 1);
end

begin
    WriteLn (Slice (Text => Str ('hello'), 1));
end
